WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.560
Tomato soup.

2
00:00:01.610 --> 00:00:04.910
Chalked in wobbly
capitals on a blackboard.

3
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:10.160
Now the same two words, in thin
gold letters on glossy black card.

4
00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:14.690
And again, in a big, bouncy
cartoon font on a children's menu.

5
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.480
The words never change.

6
00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.080
Only the look does.

7
00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:20.660
So what is the typeface telling you?

8
00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:23.800
In this mission, you'll
learn what graphology covers,

9
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:27.120
from typeface and layout
to colour and image.

10
00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:30.110
You'll ask whether a typeface
means anything on its own,

11
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.460
or only alongside the words.

12
00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:35.730
And you'll put two invented
menus side by side,

13
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.830
and read every detail.

14
00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:41.400
Your mission: work out what
the typeface is telling you.
